%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1963640d94415114d8eb3f359d5b928b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Story_End_DialogueData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueSO
  locationDialogue: Floating Islands Night
  dialogueLines:
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (Archer looses arrow after arrow, but for every spawn that drops,
      two more slip past him toward the sapling. He's breathing hard, sweat on his
      brow, backing toward the center of the garden to protect the tree with his
      own body.)
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: '(gritted teeth, nocking another arrow) There''s too many, where
      the hell did this many even come from- '
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: '(A shadow drops from above, the Shady Knight, greatsword already
      swinging before he lands. One sweep cuts through three spawns at once. He plants
      himself between Archer and the swarm without a word, cutting a bloody, efficient
      path through the rest.) '
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: '(A minute later, the last spawn falls, twitching, into the dirt.
      Silence. Just heavy breathing and the faint hum of the sapling, untouched,
      still standing.) '
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: '(sheathing the greatsword, not even winded) You''re welcome. '
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: '(catching his breath, half-glaring) I had it handled. '
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: You were standing in front of your own tree like a human shield
      with an empty quiver.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (checks, quiver is, in fact, empty) ...Timing helps.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: (looking around at the bodies, then at the sapling) This is going
      to keep happening, you know.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (wiping his brow) I know.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: You wanted a relaxing life. A garden. Quiet.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: 'That''s not what this is anymore. Not with that thing growing
      in the middle of it. '
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: So you understand what I'm about to say isn't just business talk.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: A Life Tree like this, even young, even small, it can turn dying
      land back into something that breathes again. Corrupted soil. Dead farmland.
      Places that haven't grown a thing in a generation.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: With the right care, the right hands, that sapling could give sustainability
      back to entire regions. Whole countries, eventually.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: We could help a lot of people, Archer.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (sighs, no real fight left in it) Yeah. About that
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: I'm not going to sit here and tell you you're wrong. You're not.
      I saw what a fully grown one did for an entire kingdom. I know exactly what
      this could become.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: Then-
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: I'm still retired.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: (nods, expected that) I'm not asking you to be a hero again.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: 'I''m asking you to build something with me. A company. A business. '
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: '(rubbing his face) You want to be business partners. With me.
      After a decade. '
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: 'Ex-mercenary, retired Hero, one Life Tree sapling that apparently
      attracts monsters just by existing. Frankly it writes itself. '
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (a tired huff, almost a laugh) That's not a business pitch, that's
      a tragedy waiting for a punchline.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: We're still young. Neither of us has even hit thirty.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: " Plenty of time to build something that actually matters \u2014
      on our own terms this time. No higher-ups. No orders. Just us deciding what
      it's for."
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (Archer looks back at the sapling, quiet now, glowing faintly,
      untouched by the fight around it. A long silence.)
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: ...Fine.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (holding up a hand before Shady Knight can react) But I keep the
      garden. And the tree stays here, with me. That doesn't change.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: (a small nod, almost satisfied) Wouldn't have it any other way.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: We need the tree for the business anyway.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (shaking his head, but the ghost of a smile there) Unbelievable.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: We need the tree for the business anyway.
  - characterName: Shady Knight
    dialogueLine: After the end is a new beginning.
